{"id":"00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000006:0","agent":"claude-code","sessionId":"00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001","projectPath":"C:\\Users\\dev\\Downloads\\baton","ts":"2026-11-01T20:05:53.575Z","seq":4,"kind":"prompt","text":"Read CLAUDE.md and docs/spec.md. Build apps/web: a live viewer for the daemon's WebSocket feed. No canvas yet — that's next phase, so keep components reusable as future card contents.\n\n- Sidebar: active sessions from GET /sessions (project name, last activity, live indicator).\n- Main area: one column per selected session (up to 3 side by side), each a scrolling feed. Distinct styling for prompt / reply / tool_call / tool_result. Auto-scroll that pauses when the user scrolls up, with a \"jump to latest\" button.\n- A single WebSocket connection manager hook: reconnects with backoff and resumes with lastSeq; shows connection status.\n- Render markdown in replies; keep tool lines compact and monospaced. Virtualize long feeds so 10k events don't lag.\n- Clean, minimal claymorphic design with frutiger dorfic accents.\n\nHave the daemon serve the built web app statically so `baton start` opens everything on one port.\nThinking blocks render collapsed with a ‘Show thinking’ toggle; tool results show the summary line and expand to the full output.\n\nDone = `pnpm check` passes, and with two Claude sessions running, both stream live in the browser. Use the browser preview to verify it yourself and show me a screenshot.","meta":{"sources":["typed"]}}
